 ## Background
-InfoNeRF was introduced by Mijeong Kim, Seonguk Seo, and Bohyung Han from Seoul National University in 2022 [S1]. It addresses the limitations of existing few-shot novel view synthesis methods, such as PixelNeRF [38] and class-specific methods [14, 24], which rely on features from seen images or semantic priors. InfoNeRF is distinct from explicit representation methods like octree sparsity [37] or voxel grid total variation [17] by being fully implicit and generic. It builds on the NeRF framework [21] and classical volume rendering theory [19].
